### 03.4 Replaceable Runtime Adapter

Implement a clean adapter around the exact selected runtime.

Do not hardwire model-specific execution assumptions throughout the application.

The architecture should allow a future model/runtime replacement without changing the public transcription contract.

### 03.5 Resource Awareness

The primary hardware target is an Apple M2 Mac with 8 GB unified memory.

The engine must avoid loading unnecessary model copies, unbounded queues, excessive audio buffering, and uncontrolled concurrency.

### 03.6 No Unnecessary Rewrites

Inspect existing repository architecture before creating new packages.

Reuse healthy code where appropriate.

Do not rewrite unrelated production systems, application pages, pricing engines, or existing product functionality.

Keep project-specific architectural constraints, including the 500-line source-file limit where applicable.

